+/* geni_se_select_mode(GENI_SE_DMA): the SE moves the data itself.
+ *
+ * The mode switch is more than the one bit: geni_se_irq_clear() writes 0 to
+ * SE_GSI_EVENT_EN in every mode change, geni_se_select_dma_mode() drops the
+ * FIFO watermark enables, and only then does GENI_DMA_MODE_EN come on.  Every
+ * attempt up to touch150 set the bit and left the bootloader's
+ * SE_GSI_EVENT_EN = 0xf in place, i.e. the sequencer stayed in GSI mode and
+ * handed the command to the GSI block, which has no TRE ring here.
